Subject: Break down a reused lookahead node that has no action

Read a reused lookahead node with no action as its first leaf.

The copy of the runtime of the tree-sitter-cpp fork has this repair. The fork commit is
05950d8.

After an edit, the incremental parse can take a node of the old tree as
the lookahead. If the node has no action after the reductions, the
parser detected an error and skipped the node. A fresh parse has the
first leaf of the node as the lookahead at this point. That leaf can be
a keyword that the parser reads as the word token. The two trees then
differed: in a function body, the incremental tree made `else` an ERROR,
and the fresh tree read `else` as the type of a declaration.

ts_parser__advance now replaces such a lookahead with its first leaf,
and processes the actions of the leaf again.

In the incremental test of 23,768 edits of 2,971 files, the edits whose
incremental tree differs from the fresh tree go from 54 to 24 with this
change alone, and to 15 with the error recovery changes. In the test of
43,560 edits of 1,452 snippets, they go from 19 to 11. The undo test
does not change.

The repair is not specific to a language. It makes an incremental parse give the tree of a fresh
parse in more inputs.

Risk for upstream: low.

The patch applies to the upstream tag v0.27.0, after the patches with a smaller number. The
series compiles with `-Wall -Wextra` and no warning.

The comments hold the marker "(tree-sitter-cpp fork)". Remove the marker before you send the
patch upstream.

diff -ruN a/lib/src/parser.c b/lib/src/parser.c
--- a/lib/src/parser.c	2026-09-15 19:00:45.728015329 +0200
+++ b/lib/src/parser.c	2026-09-15 19:00:45.743077499 +0200
@@ -1780,6 +1780,20 @@
       return true;
     }
 
+    // If the lookahead is a node of the old tree that has no action, replace it with its first
+    // leaf. A parse with no old tree has that leaf as the lookahead here. The leaf can be a keyword
+    // that the parse reads as the word token below. If the node stays, the parser detects an error
+    // and skips the node (tree-sitter-cpp fork).
+    if (did_reuse && lookahead.ptr && ts_subtree_child_count(lookahead) > 0) {
+      LOG("breakdown_lookahead_without_action sym:%s", TREE_NAME(lookahead));
+      ts_subtree_release(&self->tree_pool, lookahead);
+      while (reusable_node_descend(&self->reusable_node)) {}
+      lookahead = reusable_node_tree(&self->reusable_node);
+      ts_subtree_retain(lookahead);
+      ts_language_table_entry(self->language, state, ts_subtree_symbol(lookahead), &table_entry);
+      continue;
+    }
+
     // If the current lookahead token is a keyword that is not valid, but the
     // default word token *is* valid, then treat the lookahead token as the word
     // token instead.
